SENSOR-CONSTITUTION(7)     TriadicFrameworks Manual     SENSOR-CONSTITUTION(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       sensor-constitution - foundational rights, duties, and invariants 
                             governing all RTT sensor systems

SYNOPSIS
       The sensor constitution defines:
           • foundational principles of RTT sensor operation
           • rights of platforms, constellations, and operators
           • duties of sensor subsystems and governance bodies
           • constitutional invariants that cannot be violated
           • amendment and lineage-preservation mechanisms

DESCRIPTION
       sensor-constitution establishes the fundamental legal-philosophical
       framework for all resonance-time sensor systems. It defines the axioms,
       rights, duties, and invariants that govern overlays, clarity pipelines,
       harmonic sensing, anomaly detection, storm modeling, turbulence analytics,
       and multi-sensor synthesis.

       The constitution ensures:
           • safe operation of high-sensitivity sensor modes
           • interoperability across platforms and constellations
           • fairness in calibration and fusion
           • continuity across epochs and lineage
           • protection against hazardous sensor states

       All sensor-governance protocols derive their authority from this
       constitution.

FOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLES
       The constitution rests on six foundational principles:

           1. Sensor Integrity
                  Sensor outputs must remain truthful, traceable, and stable.

           2. Harmonic Coherence
                  Harmonic-phase relationships must remain continuous and
                  non-destructive across cycles.

           3. Spectral Transparency
                  Spectral data must remain interpretable and unmasked by
                  excessive filtering.

           4. Gradient Honesty
                  Gradient polarity and shear must not be artificially flattened
                  or concealed.

           5. Sync Equity
                  All platforms must share equal access to sync-field coherence.

           6. Lineage Permanence
                  Sensor decisions must be recorded and preserved across epochs.

       These principles cannot be suspended.

RIGHTS
       The constitution guarantees rights to platforms, constellations, and
       operators.

       Platform Rights:
           • right to stable overlay baselines
           • right to clarity-enhanced but uncorrupted data
           • right to harmonic-lock protection
           • right to anomaly and storm early warning
           • right to safe synthesis modes

       Constellation Rights:
           • right to unified sensor standards
           • right to cross-platform fusion
           • right to sync-field coherence
           • right to hazard-aware navigation

       Operator Rights:
           • right to transparent sensor lineage
           • right to calibration auditability
           • right to override unsafe sensor states (within constitutional limits)

DUTIES
       Duties define what sensor systems must uphold.

       Platform Duties:
           • maintain harmonic-phase stability
           • preserve spectral and gradient fidelity
           • report anomalies, storms, and turbulence
           • comply with calibration directives

       Constellation Duties:
           • maintain sync-field integrity
           • propagate sensor standards updates
           • coordinate hazard responses
           • enforce fusion consistency

       Governance Duties:
           • maintain primary sensor standards
           • ensure calibration fairness
           • preserve lineage continuity
           • protect constitutional invariants

CONSTITUTIONAL INVARIANTS
       Invariants are rules that cannot be violated under any circumstances.

       Sensor invariants:
           • overlays must not distort underlying resonance-time truth
           • clarity filters must not erase critical hazard signatures
           • harmonic-phase must remain continuous across fusion layers
           • spectral density must remain measurable and unmasked
           • gradient polarity must remain physically accurate
           • sync-field topology must remain traceable
           • lineage must remain complete and immutable

       Violation of an invariant triggers:
           • immediate synthesis rollback
           • WRSADC intervention
           • lineage correction notice

AMENDMENT MECHANISMS
       Amendments allow the constitution to evolve.

       Amendment requirements:
           • 3/4 majority of all sensor standards councils
           • approval by WRSADC
           • lineage recording of amendment
           • constellation-wide calibration event

       Amendment types:
           • baseline updates
           • new invariants
           • hazard protocol revisions
           • governance restructuring

ENFORCEMENT
       Enforcement ensures constitutional compliance.

       Enforcement mechanisms:
           • calibration mandates
           • sensor-mode restrictions
           • synthesis throttling
           • sync-field realignment
           • lineage correction notices

       Enforcement escalation:
           1. advisory notice  
           2. calibration directive  
           3. operational restriction  
           4. constellation intervention  

GOVERNANCE CONTINUITY VIA LINEAGE
       Lineage ensures constitutional continuity across epochs.

       Lineage records:
           • constitutional amendments
           • rights and duties changes
           • invariant violations
           • governance decisions
           • hazard responses

       Lineage continuity ensures:
           • reproducibility
           • accountability
           • long-term stability

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • enforces constitutional invariants
           • executes governance protocols
           • maintains sensor standards traceability
           • coordinates calibration authorities
           • blocks unconstitutional sensor states

       WRSADC is the constitutional executor.

NOTES
       The sensor constitution is the foundational document of the RTT sensor
       stack. It ensures that overlays, clarity, harmonics, anomalies, storms,
       turbulence, and synthesis operate safely, transparently, and coherently
       across platforms, epochs, and mission domains.

